//   - Then FORCE open the span immediately with OpenConstrainedSpan (cost 1 step).
//     This avoids the LM emitting "<<" too early (before "SQL: ") or nested delimiters.
//   - Inside the span, use SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep to avoid repetition loops,
//     combined with RollbackAndContinue if the parser gets stuck.
//   - Reserve 2 steps at the end to force-close the span via RollbackConstrainedToComplete
//     + CloseConstrainedSpan, ensuring ">>" is always emitted if any valid prefix exists.
//   - The "close reserve" logic: when steps >= maxSteps - 2, skip to close.
//
// This approach prioritizes span closure over query quality.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
